=== ANGLE 7a: Schur-monotonicity of measS7 in the residue-LEG vector ===

(1) does L determine measS7? (collisions = same L, different measS7)
  k=8: 332 L-collisions w/ different measS7 out of 500
     ex: L=(1, 2, 3, 4, 12, 13) from [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 12, 13, 14] and [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 7, 12, 13]
  k=9: 375 L-collisions w/ different measS7 out of 500
     ex: L=(1, 9, 3, 4, 5, 6) from [0, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, 10, 14] and [0, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 14]

(2) consec L = (1,2,3,4,5,6) is componentwise-minimal => every other L >= it.
  k=8 consec L=(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6): 200/200 configs have L >= consec componentwise
  k=9 consec L=(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6): 200/200 configs have L >= consec componentwise

(3) Schur test: order configs by measS7; check measS7 ANTI-monotone with L-majorization
  k=8: 2926/10073 majorization-comparable pairs VIOLATE 'more-spread L => less coverage'
  k=9: 3895/10355 majorization-comparable pairs VIOLATE 'more-spread L => less coverage'

(4) DECISIVE: is consec the UNIQUE measS7 max, and L the right order parameter?
  k=8 consec measS7=0.3272: 0 beat, 0 tie(diff L), out of 150
  k=9 consec measS7=0.4162: 0 beat, 0 tie(diff L), out of 150
  k=10 consec measS7=0.5045: 0 beat, 0 tie(diff L), out of 150

VERDICT: low majorization-violation + consec unique max => Schur/HS port is the wall proof.
